{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.concaveDeficit_not_excludable_on_any_grid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.concaveDeficit_not_excludable_on_any_grid","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L283-L298","doc":"**Extra data points do not help.** On a grid of any size, every\ndiscretely-convex dataset whose slopes are bounded by `c` is a linear term minus\na discretely-concave, increasing deficit. So the linear-minus-concave-deficit\nclass is not excludable by *any* finite grid, and the standing recommendation to\nextend past `A = 4` buys the ability to test **fixed shapes** and to locate the\nconvex→concave turn — not the ability to test this class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficitFun_slopes_pos_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficitFun_slopes_pos_iff","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L275-L281","doc":"The deficit is increasing on every interval exactly when `c` clears every\nsecant slope of the data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficitFun_antitone_iff_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficitFun_antitone_iff_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L259-L273","doc":"**Uniform in the grid size.** The deficit's slopes are antitone — the\ndiscrete concavity of `ψ` — exactly when the data's slopes are monotone, its\ndiscrete convexity. No hypothesis on `c`, and no dependence on `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.slope_deficitFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.slope_deficitFun","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L251-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficitFun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficitFun","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L246-L248","doc":"The deficit of `f` against the line `c·x`, on an arbitrary grid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.slope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.slope","kind":"def","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L242-L244","doc":"Secant slope of `f` across the `i`-th grid interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.ame_grid_has_concave_deficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.ame_grid_has_concave_deficit","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L220-L227","doc":"So the AME grid itself carries a concave deficit — at `c = 7`, just above its\ntop secant slope `6.7319175`. The antecedent of the main theorem is inhabited on\nthe corpus's own numbers, so nothing above is vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.ame_grid_is_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.ame_grid_is_convex","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L213-L218","doc":"The AME grid is convex through the origin: secant slopes\n`2.224566 → 2.93767725 → 6.7319175`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.ameGrid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.ameGrid","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L199-L211","doc":"The AME2020 light-nucleus grid, bond-count reading: bond counts `1, 3, 6`\nagainst `B(D)`, the isospin-averaged `B(A=3)`, and `B(⁴He)` in MeV. Exact\nrationals, no fit, no `q₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.concaveDeficit_class_not_excludable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.concaveDeficit_class_not_excludable","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L187-L197","doc":"**The consequence for the proposed exclusion.** There is no three-point test\nthat rules out the linear-minus-concave-deficit class, because membership in the\nclass *follows from* convexity — the very property the same three points are\nused to establish. Stated as: the class-membership predicate is implied by the\nantecedent, so it cannot be false on a convex dataset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.exists_concaveDeficit_of_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.exists_concaveDeficit_of_convex","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L171-L185","doc":"**The main statement.** Every convex-through-the-origin dataset *is* a\nlinear term minus a strictly increasing concave-through-the-origin deficit —\nand not for one lucky slope but for every `c` above its top secant slope. The\nreconstruction identity `fᵢ = c·xᵢ − ψᵢ` is definitional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_increasing_of_gt_secant₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_increasing_of_gt_secant₂","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L160-L169","doc":"The deficit is strictly increasing as soon as `c` clears the largest secant\nslope of the data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_concave_iff_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_concave_iff_convex","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L152-L158","doc":"**Subtracting from a line exchanges convexity for concavity, exactly.**\nThe deficit is concave through the origin iff the data is convex through the\norigin — for every `c`, with no hypothesis on `c` at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_secant₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_secant₂","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L145-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_secant₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_secant₁","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L138-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_secant₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.deficit_secant₀","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L132-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.deficit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.deficit","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L115-L126","doc":"The deficit of `d` against the linear function `c·x`: same grid, values\n`c·xᵢ − fᵢ`. This is the `ψ` of `Φ(x) = c·x − ψ(x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.IncreasingThroughOrigin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.IncreasingThroughOrigin","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L112-L113","doc":"Strictly increasing through the origin, in the secant sense. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.ConcaveThroughOrigin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.ConcaveThroughOrigin","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L109-L110","doc":"Concave through the origin: the three secant slopes decrease. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.ConvexThroughOrigin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.ConvexThroughOrigin","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L106-L107","doc":"Convex through the origin: the three secant slopes increase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.secant₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.secant₂","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Secant slope across the second interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.secant₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.secant₁","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L100-L101","doc":"Secant slope across the first interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.secant₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.secant₀","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L97-L98","doc":"Secant slope from the origin to the first point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.hx₂₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.hx₂₃","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.hx₁₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.hx₁₂","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.hx₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.hx₁","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.f₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.f₃","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.f₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.f₂","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.f₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.f₁","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.x₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.x₃","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.x₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.x₂","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.x₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.x₁","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.GridData","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConcaveDeficitNonExclusion.lean#L78-L91","doc":"Three data points on a positive, strictly increasing grid, read together\nwith the origin. `f` is the value; the grid `x` is shared by everything built\nfrom it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}